# winewayland: Keep undecorated popups owned by a fullscreen window as subsurfaces.
# https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/12754 state=opened
# Old DirectDraw games such as Diablo show their menus in undecorated `WS_POPUP` windows owned by their fullscreen main window. Each of them became a separate fullscreen `xdg_toplevel`, fighting with its owner over focus and stacking. This keeps such popups unmanaged, so that they are attached as subsurfaces of their owner, and makes pointer locking and mouse input work while one of these subsurfaces is the foreground window.

### How to reproduce

Diablo (1996, DirectDraw, 640x480) on winewayland. Its main window is a fullscreen `WS_POPUP`, and its menus and dialogs are undecorated `WS_POPUP` windows owned by that main window. The game hides the cursor and clips it while they are shown.

Before this, starting the game and opening a menu shows:

- each menu becomes its own fullscreen `xdg_toplevel`, which competes with the main window for focus and stacking;
- mouse clicks go to the main window instead of the menu under the cursor;
- the pointer lock never activates while a menu is the foreground window, so relative motion is turned off and the cursor stops moving.

### Tested on

- [labwc 0.20.3](https://github.com/labwc/labwc), one 3840x2160 output at scale 2, Intel UHD 630.
- Games: Diablo, StarCraft, Warcraft II.
- Not tested on any other compositor.
- Not tested in a Wine virtual desktop.

The testing was done on a branch that also contains !12751, !12755 and one further winewayland commit that is not part of this MR (see below).

### Known limitation

Subsurfaces are composited by the compositor, so nothing invalidates the owner when a popup subsurface is hidden. Diablo draws its dialogs into the main window's DirectDraw surface and relies on a `WM_PAINT` for the uncovered area, so a closed dialog can leave a stale image behind. I have a fix for that, but it makes the owner behave like pre-Windows 8 (non-composited) Windows, so I left it out of this MR.
--- dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c
+++ dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_pointer.c
@@ -122,6 +122,22 @@ static HWND wayland_pointer_get_focused_hwnd(void)
     return hwnd;
 }
 
+/* While the pointer is locked, the cursor moves independently of the
+ * Wayland pointer focus, and may be over another window (e.g. an owned
+ * popup) than the focused one. Let the server find the window under the
+ * cursor then, instead of restricting the input to the focused window. */
+static HWND wayland_pointer_get_input_hwnd(HWND hwnd)
+{
+    struct wayland_pointer *pointer = &process_wayland.pointer;
+    BOOL relative_mode;
+
+    pthread_mutex_lock(&pointer->mutex);
+    relative_mode = pointer->relative_mode;
+    pthread_mutex_unlock(&pointer->mutex);
+
+    return relative_mode ? NULL : hwnd;
+}
+
 static void pointer_handle_motion_internal(wl_fixed_t sx, wl_fixed_t sy)
 {
